8a2e58cab15f256766976451ac08d53a5e","text":"Scale Exercises - Section II, Level 15\n\nMajor Scale Three-Note Rolling Sequence: Two-Octave Six-String Neck Ladder                                                                                                                                    26 triplets. One unbroken pick cycle.\n\nCarry the Level 14 overlap pattern across all six strings and both octaves before shifting one fret.\n\n     1. Expand the sequence                                                                    2. Preserve the pick cycle                                                               3. Shift only after the cell\n\n     Use 13 ascending triplets and 13 descending triplets.                                     Alternate continuously through every group, string                                       Complete all 78 notes, return to the low root, release\n     The scale now spans positions 1-15.                                                       crossing, octave, high-root turn, and frame shift.                                       pressure, and move the full frame exactly one fret.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n      Worked example - A major at low-E fret 5                                                                                                                                                                            Session protocol\n\n      Scale tones: A B C# D E F# G# A B C# D E F# G# A. High root repeats at the turn.                                                                                                                                               Master the 13\n      UP: 123 | 234 | ... | 13-14-15     DOWN: 15-14-13 | 14-13-12 | ... | 321                                                                                                                                               1       ascending triplets in A\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     major.\n\n      ASCENDING - 13 TRIPLETS / 39 NOTES                                                                                                                                                                                             Master the 13\n\n      Deg|1--2--3--|2--3--4--|3--4--5--|4--5--6--|5--6--7--|6--7--8--|7--8--9--|8--9--10-|9--10-11-|10-11-12-|11-12-13-|12-13-14-|13-14-15-|                                                                                 2       descending triplets in A\n      Fng|2--4--1--|4--1--2--|1--2--4--|2--4--1--|4--1--3--|1--3--4--|3--4--1--|4--1--3--|1--3--4--|3--4--2--|4--2--4--|2--4--1--|4--1--2--|                                                                                         major.\n      e  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|------4--|---4--5--|\n      B  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|------5--|---5--7--|5--7-----|7--------|\n      G  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|------4--|---4--6--|4--6--7--|6--7-----|7--------|---------|---------|\n      D  |---------|---------|---------|------4--|---4--6--|4--6--7--|6--7-----|7--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\n      A  |------4--|---4--5--|4--5--7--|5--7-----|7--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|                                                                                         Link both halves; do not\n      E  |5--7-----|7--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|                                                                                         reset at the high root.\n      DESCENDING - 13 TRIPLETS / 39 NOTES                                                                                                                                                                                    3\n\n      Deg|15-14-13-|14-13-12-|13-12-11-|12-11-10-|11-10-9--|10-9--8--|9--8--7--|8--7--6--|7--6--5--|6--5--4--|5--4--3--|4--3--2--|3--2--1--|\n      Fng|2--1--4--|1--4--2--|4--2--4--|2--4--3--|4--3--1--|3--1--4--|1--4--3--|4--3--1--|3--1--4--|1--4--2--|4--2--1--|2--1--4--|1--4--2--|\n      e  |5--4-----|4--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\n      B  |------7--|---7--5--|7--5-----|5--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|                                                                                         Start 15-20 BPM below\n      G  |---------|---------|------7--|---7--6--|7--6--4--|6--4-----|4--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|                                                                                         your clean Level 14\n      D  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|------7--|---7--6--|7--6--4--|6--4-----|4--------|---------|---------|---------|                                                                                 4\n      A  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|------7--|---7--5--|7--5--4--|5--4-----|4--------|                                                                                         tempo.\n      E  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|------7--|---7--5--|\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     Use 2-3 rungs; pause\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                             5       one beat after each\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     cell.\n\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     Remove the pause;\n      KEY ROUTE              A -> Bb -> B -> C -> Db -> D -> Eb -> E -> F -> Gb -> G -> Ab -> A, then reverse.                                                                                                               6       connect the full route\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     both ways.\n      AUDIT                  Hear 26 equal triplets; make string crossings, octave roots, and one-fret shifts invisible.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSection II now combines overlapping triplets with the complete two-octave major-scale frame.                                                                                                                                                        Page 1 of 10","text_sha256":"c1224055932bc5bc006d55d555257f81c39b824942fc13ae9fc81722c242732f"},"L15-TXT1-60-67":{"first_line":60,"format":"txt","last_line":67,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/TXT version/Scale_Exercises_Section_II_Level_15_Major_Scale_Three_Note_Rolling_Sequence_Two_Octave_Six_String_Neck_Ladder.txt","sha256":"896937c0d5040c8e7590364433e141bbe7f6da419e063a8ed2590666d5a2c514","text":"Use eighth-note triplets: one three-note group per beat. Begin 15-20 BPM below your clean Level 14 tempo.\nFirst master the 13 ascending triplets in A major, then the 13 descending triplets. Link them without\nrestarting the pick cycle and make the two high-root notes equal in length and volume. Next use 2-3\nneighboring rungs and pause one beat after each 78-note cell while moving the complete frame one fret.\nRepeat with both pick starts. Remove the pause, connect the ladder, reverse after the fret-17 cell, and\nreturn to fret 5. Add 2 BPM after three clean round trips. Reduce 4-6 BPM after two errors, a broken triplet\npulse, a missed B-string offset, dragged shift noise, or rising tension. Advance after the complete route\nis clean with both pick starts on two separate days.","text_sha256":"e9a6eb4bd14e4fd053414c395449415a1f6feee6d3d5570b02265de01fe2dd4b"},"L15-TXT1-70-91":{"first_line":70,"format":"txt","last_line":91,"path":"Notes/music/guitar project/TXT version/Scale_Exercises_Section_II_Level_15_Major_Scale_Three_Note_Rolling_Sequence_Two_Octave_Six_String_Neck_Ladder.txt","sha256":"896937c0d5040c8e7590364433e141bbe7f6da419e063a8ed2590666d5a2c514","text":"RUNG 01 OF 13 - A MAJOR - ROOT ON LOW E FRET 5 - FRAME 4-7\nScale tones across two octaves: A B C# D E F# G# A B C# D E F# G# A\n78-note cell: 13 ascending rolling triplets, repeat the high root at the turn, then 13 descending triplets.\nASCENDING - 13 TRIPLETS / 39 NOTES\nDeg|1--2--3--|2--3--4--|3--4--5--|4--5--6--|5--6--7--|6--7--8--|7--8--9--|8--9--10-|9--10-11-|10-11-12-|11-12-13-|12-13-14-|13-14-15-|\nFng|2--4--1--|4--1--2--|1--2--4--|2--4--1--|4--1--3--|1--3--4--|3--4--1--|4--1--3--|1--3--4--|3--4--2--|4--2--4--|2--4--1--|4--1--2--|\ne  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|------4--|---4--5--|\nB  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|------5--|---5--7--|5--7-----|7--------|\nG  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|------4--|---4--6--|4--6--7--|6--7-----|7--------|---------|---------|\nD  |---------|---------|---------|------4--|---4--6--|4--6--7--|6--7-----|7--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nA  |------4--|---4--5--|4--5--7--|5--7-----|7--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nE  |5--7-----|7--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nDESCENDING - 13 TRIPLETS / 39 NOTES\nDeg|15-14-13-|14-13-12-|13-12-11-|12-11-10-|11-10-9--|10-9--8--|9--8--7--|8--7--6--|7--6--5--|6--5--4--|5--4--3--|4--3--2--|3--2--1--|\nFng|2--1--4--|1--4--2--|4--2--4--|2--4--3--|4--3--1--|3--1--4--|1--4--3--|4--3--1--|3--1--4--|1--4--2--|4--2--1--|2--1--4--|1--4--2--|\ne  |5--4-----|4--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nB  |------7--|---7--5--|7--5-----|5--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nG  |---------|---------|------7--|---7--6--|7--6--4--|6--4-----|4--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|\nD  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|------7--|---7--6--|7--6--4--|6--4-----|4--------|---------|---------|---------|\nA  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|------7--|---7--5--|7--5--4--|5--4-----|4--------|\nE  |---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|------7--|---7--5--|\nFinish on the low root, release pressure, and move the entire frame one fret in the route direction.","text_sha256":"7b761da2f6ac68b3d2acd2956a02d834c73c53ed4e7fa162c8f478a3593e0e53"}}}
